{
  "slug": "zulrah",
  "note": "Confirms the parser's ambiguous-heading guess on the \"Mutagens\" heading (revid 15285439): its 3 rows (Flax 10/249, Tanzanite mutagen 1/13107, Magma mutagen 1/13107) sit at heterogeneous denominators and carry no Pre-roll/Tertiary/Secondary keyword, so build-tables.ts's final fallback flagged it needs_review and defaulted to a preroll guess. Checked directly against https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Zulrah: the section's own prose describes a genuine two-stage nested gate -- \"There is a 10/249 chance to roll on the flax table, followed by a 10/2,632 chance to roll on the mutagen sub-table\" -- i.e. a mutagen REPLACES flax's own outcome on a tiny slice of the SAME roll, not a separate access roll with its own total to partition (unlike this boss's own herb/seed-style tables elsewhere in the corpus, there is no single stated total these three rows sum to). The wiki's own footnotes confirm each row's displayed rarity (10/249, 1/13107, 1/13107) is already the item's fully-resolved, final per-roll probability -- \"the exact rarity is 10/249 * 5244/5264 per roll\" for Flax and \"10/249 * 10/5264 per roll\" for each mutagen -- so this is exactly what `preroll` mode already computes: sequential trials at each row's own independent stated rate, first hit wins, same shape as this boss's own already-shipped Weapons/Runes/etc. tables and identical in kind to e.g. Alchemical Hydra's unique preroll table (data/bosses/alchemical-hydra.json's \"pre-roll\" heading). The guess was correct; this override changes nothing structurally and exists only to move the heading off the ambiguous-guess gate with a human confirmation on record. Every table is otherwise identical to the generated document.",
